            "That very morning a gentleman came into the shop. He tried on the new shoes, and they fitted him perfectly. He was so pleased that he paid twice the usual price. With the money the shoemaker bought enough leather for two pairs of shoes.",
            "That evening he cut out the leather for two pairs and left the pieces on his bench, just as before. And in the morning there they were, two pairs of beautiful shoes, finished and polished and standing side by side.",
            "Two customers came in that day and bought them both, and they paid well. Now the shoemaker could buy leather for four pairs. And so it went on, night after night. Whatever he cut out in the evening was finished by the morning.",
            "Soon the little shop was busy from morning till night. People came from all over the town to buy the finest shoes they had ever worn. The shoemaker and his wife were never hungry again, and there was always a warm fire in the grate.",
            "One evening, not long before Christmas, the shoemaker sat by the fire with his wife. I should so like to know who is helping us, he said. Let us stay up tonight and watch. His wife agreed, and they hid behind the coats in the corner.",
