            "Then the elves lined the shoes up neatly, jumped down from the bench, and ran out of the door into the frosty night. The candle flickered, and the workshop was quiet again. The shoemaker and his wife looked at each other in wonder.",
            "In the morning the shoemaker's wife said, Those little elves have made us so happy, and yet they have nothing to keep them warm. I shall sew each of them a little shirt, a coat and a pair of trousers, and I will knit them warm socks.",
            "That is a fine idea, said the shoemaker. And I shall make each of them a pair of tiny shoes. So they both set to work. They sewed and knitted and stitched all day, and by the evening everything was ready.",
