            "Once upon a time, high above the hills and the fields, the North Wind and the Sun shared the wide blue sky. The North Wind lived in the cold north, where the snow lay deep. The Sun lived in the bright middle of the sky and shone down on everyone.",
            "Most days they got along very well. But the North Wind was a boastful fellow, and he liked to show off. One morning he puffed out his cheeks and said, I am the strongest thing in the whole sky. Nobody is as strong as me.",
            "The Sun smiled her calm, golden smile. Strength comes in many kinds, she said. Perhaps you are strong in one way, and I am strong in another.",
