            "Easy! laughed the North Wind. I shall have that cloak off in a moment. You may as well give up now.",
            "The Sun went behind a cloud to watch, and the North Wind took a deep, deep breath. Then he blew. A cold gust swept down over the hills and along the road. The grass bent flat, the leaves spun from the hedges, and the traveller's hat nearly flew away.",
            "The traveller shivered. My, it has turned chilly, he said. He held his hat on with one hand, and with the other he pulled his cloak more tightly around him.",
            "The North Wind frowned. He took an even deeper breath and blew harder. The wind whooshed and whistled across the fields. The trees bowed low, the sheep huddled together by the wall, and the clouds raced across the sky.",
            "But the harder the North Wind blew, the more tightly the traveller held his cloak. He wrapped it twice around himself, tucked his chin into the collar and leaned forward into the wind. He was not going to let it go.",
            "The North Wind blew and blew until he was quite out of breath. He blew until his cheeks ached and the sky was full of tumbling clouds. But still the cloak stayed on. At last the North Wind gave up and sank down, puffing, behind a hill.",
            "Your turn, he grumbled. But you will not do any better.",
