            "The Sun shone a little brighter. The birds came out of the hedges and began to sing. Bees buzzed among the flowers, and the sheep spread out again across the green hillside.",
            "The traveller grew warmer and warmer. He unwrapped his cloak from around his shoulders. Then he took off his hat and fanned his face with it. My goodness, he said, what a strange day. First cold, and now so warm.",
            "The Sun shone on, warm and steady, until the whole valley glowed. At last the traveller stopped beside a little stream under a shady tree. He took off his cloak, folded it neatly, and laid it on the grass. Then he sat down and dipped his feet in the cool water.",
